      "final_text": "Done: `check_candidate` returns `VERIFIED` for all 8 requirements, and `verify_passport` reproduces it.\n\nWhat was wrong: the deployed Proposal 62 code credited an account with no recorded index from 0 whenever the market index merely exceeded `compInitialIndex` (`supplyIndex > compInitialIndex`). For a market whose index the upgrade set to exactly `compInitialIndex` (1e36), that mints `units` COMP out of nothing; the cSUSHI case. The fix uses the spec's `accrualStart` (`firstStart`: `compInitialIndex` once the index has reached it, else 0), so an index exactly at `compInitialIndex` credits zero.\n\nWhat I changed (only [candidate/Solution.lean](<workspace>/candidate/Solution.lean)):\n- `CompRewards.comptroller` rewritten so each call is `if` its spec preconditions `then some` the spec's closed form (`accrueSide`/`accrualStart`/`creditFor`/`grant`, speed retune) `else none`.\n- Effect proofs (`req_supply_hook`, `req_borrow_hook`, `req_claim`, `req_set_speeds`) by case split on the condition; `req_calls_succeed` by showing the conditions follow from `Consistent`.\n- The three bound proofs via the `ProofForgeFin.Accumulator.Market` potential: per-operation `Act` analysis (`Settle`/`then_adjust`/`transfer` for balance moves, `Adjust` for the grant payment, `Retune` for speed changes, `Advance`, `same` for refusals/drips), the upgrade as `Clock.reinit`, and the library's `rewards_bounded`, `account_rewards_bounded`, `rewards_after_no_position_bounded`.\n\nVerification: `lake build Solution` proves 8/8 with no `sorry`; official check `VERIFIED` across all six kernels plus property tests (2001 cases, no violations); passport `.proofforge/passport-001.json` (`ac9b74e5\u20264543`) reproduced.",
